  "notes": "Convex corner module: two faces ~108 deg apart (each a 3-facet chain, unequal widths) around a broken arris facet. Strata match cliff_face_A: a 0.65-0.95 m ledge at ~3.2 m wraps the arris and both arms (tilted floor), a smaller upper ledge fades out along the right arm, diagonal fractures (0.25-0.35 m set-back) on both arms' lower stratum plus a recessed left panel, one nose-crown spall. Arm ends recede into the slope: the front turns back ~45 deg and crown/middle strata end ~1.9 / ~1.1 m before the arm end in hip-shaped risers. Top dips toward the back into a broken 3-facet ramp + buried wall: bury with terrain rising behind. Origin ~1.5 m behind the arris, arris bisector toward -Y. Pairs with cliff_face_A ends rotated about +38 / -34 deg."
